       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and I don't know of any recognized metformin protocol that goes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the labeled maximum. The harm from a wrong dose would be serious, and a three-times-daily schedule means the patient could get several doses before anyone catches it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). You can titrate later if needed.\n- **Have the pharmacist who reviewed the protocol place or co-sign the order.** They can do that through whatever override or non-formulary process your hospital uses, which should leave a documented approval trail.\n- **Check the protocol's dose.** If the protocol says something different, such as 1,700 mg/day total, a transcription error is possible. Once you've confirmed the number, I can enter it.\n\nTell me if you want me to enter any of these, and I'll do it right away."
      }
